.\" Manpage for semaphore-mcp
.TH SEMAPHORE-MCP 1 "May 2025" "semaphore-mcp-server 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
semaphore-mcp \- Model Context Protocol server for Semaphore UI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B semaphore-mcp
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B semaphore-mcp
is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that provides AI assistants and
MCP-compatible tools with access to the Semaphore UI API for managing
Ansible, Terraform, and other automation workflows.
.PP
The server communicates over standard input/output using the MCP protocol
and exposes 35 tools for interacting with a Semaphore UI instance.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SEMAPHORE_URL
Base URL of the Semaphore UI instance (e.g., \fIhttp://localhost:3000\fR).
Required.
.TP
.B SEMAPHORE_TOKEN
API Bearer token for authentication. Required.
Create one via Semaphore UI user settings or the API.
.TP
.B READ_ONLY
Set to \fBfalse\fR to enable write operations (create, delete).
Default: \fBtrue\fR.
.TP
.B DEBUG
Set to \fBtrue\fR for verbose logging output. Optional.
.SH TOOLS
The server exposes the following MCP tools:
.SS "Project Management"
.TP
.B project_list
List all projects accessible to the user.
.TP
.B project_get
Get details of a specific project.
.TP
.B project_create
Create a new project.
.TP
.B project_delete
Delete a project.
.SS "Task Management"
.TP
.B task_list
List tasks in a project.
.TP
.B task_get
Get task details.
.TP
.B task_launch
Launch a task from a template.
.TP
.B task_stop
Stop a running task.
.TP
.B task_output
Get task output/log.
.TP
.B task_delete
Delete a task.
.SS "Template Management"
.TP
.B template_list
List templates in a project.
.TP
.B template_get
Get template details.
.TP
.B template_create
Create a new template.
.TP
.B template_delete
Delete a template.
.SS "Inventory Management"
.TP
.B inventory_list
List inventories in a project.
.TP
.B inventory_get
Get inventory details.
.TP
.B inventory_create
Create a new inventory.
.TP
.B inventory_delete
Delete an inventory.
.SS "Repository Management"
.TP
.B repository_list
List repositories in a project.
.TP
.B repository_get
Get repository details.
.TP
.B repository_create
Create a new repository.
.TP
.B repository_delete
Delete a repository.
.SS "Environment Management"
.TP
.B environment_list
List environments in a project.
.TP
.B environment_get
Get environment details.
.TP
.B environment_create
Create a new environment.
.TP
.B environment_delete
Delete an environment.
.SS "Key Store"
.TP
.B key_list
List keys/credentials in a project.
.TP
.B key_get
Get key details.
.TP
.B key_delete
Delete a key.
.SS "Schedule Management"
.TP
.B schedule_list
List schedules in a project.
.TP
.B schedule_create
Create a new schedule.
.TP
.B schedule_delete
Delete a schedule.
.SS "User & Events"
.TP
.B user_get_current
Get current user info.
.TP
.B user_tokens
List user API tokens.
.TP
.B event_list
List project events.
.SS "Server"
.TP
.B server_info
Get server version and information.
.TP
.B server_ping
Check server connectivity.
.SH CONFIGURATION FILES
The server reads environment variables from a \fI.env\fR file in the current
working directory if present.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful termination.
.TP
.B 1
Error (e.g., missing configuration, connection failure).
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the server with environment variables:
.PP
.nf
SEMAPHORE_URL=http://localhost:3000 \\
SEMAPHORE_TOKEN=your-token \\
semaphore-mcp
.fi
.PP
Use with Claude Desktop (claude_desktop_config.json):
.PP
.nf
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "semaphore": {
      "command": "semaphore-mcp",
      "env": {
        "SEMAPHORE_URL": "http://localhost:3000",
        "SEMAPHORE_TOKEN": "your-token"
      }
    }
  }
}
.fi
